{
  "id": "hawzi_tlemcen",
  "name": "Hawzi (Tlemcen urban sung poetry)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Urban sung-poetry genre of Tlemcen, set to dialectal Arabic poems by Tlemcen poets such as Ibn Msayeb and Bensahla and sung with the instruments and modes of the gharnati Andalusi school, but as freer single songs rather than full nuba suites. Cheikha Tetma, Abdelkrim Dali and Nouri Koufi are among its recorded singers. The fiddle card stands in for the upright-held kamanja, the tar_frame_drum card for the small jingled tar and the hand-drum card for the derbouka goblet drum.",
  "recipe": "classic North African early-1950s hawzi, ballad Poetry, med east poetic branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. oud, kwitra, fiddle, tar frame drum, hand drum source unspecified. stone plaster medina room. large-diaphragm condenser, German V72 tube pre, German tube console. tape 15ips.",
